model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "AppPages event databases enable the existing grouped SQL transport; other Worker event databases keep their prior mode. Pool AppPages queries group independent SQL, and connection-list concurrency is limited to fenced SelectionReadFacts reads. Every live authority predicate and both before/after fences remain. Independent control, exact source and retained presentation reads may overlap, but no authorization verdict is cached and no data escapes a refused control read. Speculative source reads can still run when control later refuses or omits their accounts. The full public five-account query retains all exact source executions and reports within 80 sequential SQL wire waits under injected query latency. A protocol observer starts for the declared pool-setup fixture, excludes connection login, captures pipelined statements, and preserves the existing presentation-path bound. An account's health reads the account beside its apps, checks and report, so the account's own failure reports first; its binding and driver reads, which need the stored account, then share one round trip inside a statement group and stay sequential outside one."
    }
  }
}
